{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_2c835b02424166d36c3e0b4d4144cd2cbdd3838ef07d3a43068858de89b78048"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Results are accessible via two page types: a /result/ page suited to local use, and a /survey/ page that hides method names and randomizes review order."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3e79cb9524a663e1123804584369004a0e795290949dd97a8bfba7e731eab4c2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The documented reproduction workflow involves decompressing the GPT cache, syncing the ARIES dataset, building and entering the review_worker Docker container, and running paper_align_eval_repro.py per config directory."},{"claim_ids":["clm_410f8c64d8d2a41acdbd4252ef064d2ad8bbb3ca71df8615e749353624829e11"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The repository contains code for the web interface used in the MARG user study and serves as a demo of the multi-agent review generation system for scientific papers."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7590d98a2276240f8b314c203826b7ef66a0fd4ce1d63a4adc32e5597ba110af"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Submitted papers are reviewed by three methods: SARG-B (\"barebones\"), LiZCa (\"liang_etal\"), and MARG-S (\"multi_agent_specialized\")."},{"claim_ids":["clm_870e0816c05087d97250011ddac8bd78c2106fce4922b1f6833c77e3ff515c14"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The demo runs as a web application on localhost port 8080, where papers can be submitted on the main page and results viewed at a /list-results page."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a1eac8139e923f61c2d04ba50ac18d766ac0c850117cfe846ed9c4168f04e499"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"By default the reproduction pipeline uses the cached GPT responses from the paper to ensure reproducibility; the cache can be disabled by deleting the sqlite file or editing align_config.json."},{"claim_ids":["clm_cb5edc2ccfb25e6b2cfd22e0e0285a1a306ea6197ef2249e7bd00039bc1a8a19"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Running the demo requires Docker (and possibly docker-compose), plus a .env file with an OpenAI API key; AWS credentials are optional and only needed for email notifications via Amazon SES."},{"claim_ids":["clm_dca51674df8f390cf11f0a6b23e09f60d1f77f6c3157e11516fb76e3c0f8f9d9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The code is licensed under Apache 2.0 and copyrighted 2023 by the Allen Institute for Artificial Intelligence."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ed5cd658a9c052d71acbd49d5a3cc81761eaaa64c0d1b786a1f28551858f56f0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Alignment/metrics code for reproducing the paper's Table 2 experiments lives in review_worker/paper_align_eval_repro.py, with experiment configs and outputs under review_worker/data/paper_align_eval/."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f30c794b517ee1802d239a08bd3ed92db84bbccb9f1576bc62862149e6e99217"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Email notifications on review completion are handled through Amazon SES, with the outgoing address configured via OUTGOING_EMAIL in review_worker/run_reviewgen.py."},{"claim_ids":["clm_fa6ba8e7b398de003ebffb5fe8f30b81ed31beb7d4e55f5bac9bed628f8af3d2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Reproducing experiments requires the ARIES dataset (paper texts and human reviewer data) downloaded from a public S3 bucket, plus a provided compressed GPT request cache (gpt3_cache.sqlite.xz)."}],"claim_ids":["clm_2c835b02424166d36c3e0b4d4144cd2cbdd3838ef07d3a43068858de89b78048","clm_3e79cb9524a663e1123804584369004a0e795290949dd97a8bfba7e731eab4c2","clm_410f8c64d8d2a41acdbd4252ef064d2ad8bbb3ca71df8615e749353624829e11","clm_7590d98a2276240f8b314c203826b7ef66a0fd4ce1d63a4adc32e5597ba110af","clm_870e0816c05087d97250011ddac8bd78c2106fce4922b1f6833c77e3ff515c14","clm_a1eac8139e923f61c2d04ba50ac18d766ac0c850117cfe846ed9c4168f04e499","clm_cb5edc2ccfb25e6b2cfd22e0e0285a1a306ea6197ef2249e7bd00039bc1a8a19","clm_dca51674df8f390cf11f0a6b23e09f60d1f77f6c3157e11516fb76e3c0f8f9d9","clm_ed5cd658a9c052d71acbd49d5a3cc81761eaaa64c0d1b786a1f28551858f56f0","clm_f30c794b517ee1802d239a08bd3ed92db84bbccb9f1576bc62862149e6e99217","clm_fa6ba8e7b398de003ebffb5f